comments.body:
@Webifi 
Would you please close this issue?  
There are so many similar experiences, where a transmitter battery drains faster than expected.  Dexcom has a warranty that covers early battery failure.

> In this case, x-drip seems to be able to put the G5 (and G6 for that matter) in to a mode that consumes more power.

xDrip cannot put the transmitter into any mode. It can only starts and stops a sensor. That is the only "write" access to the transmitter. In between, it just reads the data every five minutes. I really don't see any causality that xDrip is responsible for a higher power consumption of the transmitter.

@jamorham Any further comments to this issue?
